    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0295" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 T 71/155: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Helsingfors</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haynes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-25T14:00:00+01:39"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1919,
                                2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:52 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>254. Tredwell with twenty-one others leaving Moscow. Expected to arrive Finland
                    few days.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d163-f1"/> I will either go to border or ask
                    Imbrie meet him and facilitate journey to Helsingfors. Not sent Paris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Haynes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="48" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Consul Tredwell crossed the frontier into Finland Apr. 27.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
